;; THE GATE MAP (P11.7, D528; D524, D550). Read by `bb ci plan`, `bb ci core`, `bb ci shards`, `bb ci verify-plan`, `bb ci map-coverage` (tools/ci.clj) and, through them, by
;; the workflows: pr.yml (a pull request) and verify.yml (a push to main, weekly, on demand).
;;
;;   :core    the FAST CORE: runs on every pull request and every push to main, whatever the change, one command after another (`bb ci core`). :secs is measured on the
;;            maintainer's machine (D528); :gate names the gate it is, so the plan does not schedule it a second time.
;;   :groups  names for sets of gates, used as `@name` in an entry.
;;   :shards  EVERY gate, once, in the shard it runs in on the full run (verify.yml reads this through `bb ci verify-plan`, whose planned shards have the shape of `bb ci shards`;
;;            the pull request plan runs the shards that hold a planned gate). :own-job: the shard is not part of the matrix (the `unit` gate has a job of its own, one per arm).
;;   :version-files  the files `bb version set` rewrites (tools/version.clj holds the list; `bb ci map-coverage` fails when the two differ). A diff of one of these that changes
;;            nothing but the version strings those patterns find is a VERSION-ONLY change: the plan drops the path, so the release bump plans no gate (D550).
;;   :archives  globs of the files the release archives (the CLI, C library and pod, D541, D542) are built from: a change to one rebuilds them on main. A version change rebuilds
;;            them too (the archives carry the version), whatever the paths. A glob that matches no tracked file is dead and fails.
;;   :fast    the gates that take `--fast` (`bb gates --fast G...` runs `bb G --fast`): what the variant leaves out, and the measured seconds, full and fast. kin/scripts/gates
;;            lists the same set in `fast_gates`; `bb ci map-coverage` fails if the two differ.
;;   :map     path glob -> the gates a change to it calls for, ADDED UP over every entry that matches. EVERY tracked path must match at least one entry; an entry that matches
;;            none is dead and fails too. `[]` is an answer: the path needs no gate beyond the fast core (a document, a recorder, a report). :hosts names the host
;;            arms (java csharp c pod wasm; go for the unit gate's Go arm) the change touches: a --fast run leaves those arms out unless the plan names them (EMON_FAST_HOSTS), Rust and Go always run
;;            in every gate but unit.
;;            Globs: `**/` any directories, `**` anything, `*` within a name, `?` one character, `{a,b}`.
;;
;; A map is a CLAIM about dependence, not a proof. A path mapped narrowly misses a gate that the weekly and release runs (every gate, in full) still catch; a PR that touches
;; the generated logic of a family names the replay gates whose digests hold its outputs, and the rest is the weekly run's. D528 says which way each family leans.
{:core
 [{:id "check"         :cmd ["bb" "check"]                        :gate "check"         :secs 19  :why "one source, four languages, one answer: the whole generate-compile-run path"}
  {:id "drift"         :cmd ["bb" "drift"]                        :gate "drift"         :secs 61  :why "the committed generated tree is what the sources say"}
  {:id "hosts"         :cmd ["bb" "hosts"]                        :gate "hosts"         :secs 3   :why "the four host trees agree"}
  {:id "lang-test"     :cmd ["bb" "lang-test"]                    :gate "lang-test"     :secs 1   :why "the generator's own refusals (emit-ascii, defenum, defctx, fd): under a second"}
  {:id "api-diff"      :cmd ["bb" "api-diff"]                     :gate "api-diff"      :secs 2   :why "the public API is the frozen one (D527)"}
  {:id "release-audit" :cmd ["bb" "release-audit"]                :gate "release-audit" :secs 1   :why "licences, inventory and notices (D526)"}
  {:id "version"       :cmd ["bb" "version" "--check" "@version"]                       :secs 1   :why "every manifest equals version.edn (D525)"}
  {:id "release-notes-selftest"  :cmd ["bb" "release-notes" "--self-test"]                    :secs 1   :why "the release notes tool's parsing and rendering (D547)"}
  {:id "release-verify-selftest" :cmd ["bb" "release-verify" "--self-test"]                   :secs 1   :why "the publish job's three checks decide correctly on synthetic facts (D547)"}
  {:id "release-ops-selftest"    :cmd ["bb" "release-ops" "--self-test"]                      :secs 1   :why "next, draft, archive, verdict, fetch-archives, attach and summary decide correctly (D547, D550)"}
  {:id "publish-selftest"        :cmd ["bb" "publish" "--self-test"]                          :secs 1   :why "the registry publishers' idempotence checks and parsers (D547)"}
  {:id "docs"          :cmd ["bb" "docs" "--check"]                                    :secs 1   :why "the documentation is what `bb docs` generates: the option, limit and Model tables, the host API indexes, the snippets; every code block is a compiled snippet or marked unverified (D549)"}
  {:id "docs-selftest" :cmd ["bb" "docs" "--self-test"]                                :secs 1   :why "the documentation checks catch a stale table, a stale snippet, an unmarked code block, a dead link and a stale version (D549)"}
  {:id "site"          :cmd ["bb" "site" "--check" "--no-demo"]                         :secs 2   :why "the site builds; every catalogue is complete, links, fragments, HTML, sizes and contrast hold; demo and pdfium renders skip loudly (D629); measured 1.9s with warm dependencies"}
  {:id "site-selftest" :cmd ["bb" "site" "--self-test"]                                :secs 1   :why "planted translation, placeholder, link, fragment, HTML, size and contrast failures are caught (D629)"}
  {:id "ci-selftest"   :cmd ["bb" "ci" "map-coverage" "--self-test"]                  :secs 32  :why "the planner: globs, planted map failures, the plan, the version-only rule (the release bump plans no gate) and what verify.yml runs (D528, D550)"}
  {:id "ci-coverage"   :cmd ["bb" "ci" "coverage"]                                    :secs 1   :why "the gate map covers the tree, every gate is in a shard, every workflow task exists, every replay gate re-derives (includes rederive --check)"}]

