 ;; :full and :fast are wall seconds on the maintainer's machine, warm caches, one gate at a time, `corpus/` absent (as on a pull request), while the machine was shared (load average
 ;; 15 to 110): read them as orders of magnitude, not as runner times. A cold GitHub runner adds the toolchain builds (Java, .NET, C, the pod), which the --fast variants mostly skip.
 ;; Gates NOT here have no --fast variant and run in full on a pull request, each under three minutes: plan 7, embedders 9, asset 37, png-check 3, fuzz 170 (already a fixed-seed small budget), pdfium-wasm (arm A, the Rust and Go replays of six small transcripts, is the whole gate wherever pdfium's wasm build is not fetched: a runner does not fetch it, so no variant is needed; arm B, the live build in Node, runs only where `bb pdfium-fetch --platform wasm` was run).
